        "original_id": "225d9823-064e-5547-b8f7-e03792127545",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy Nungesser, Kip Holden, John Bel Edwards, David Vitter, Bill Cassidy, Susan Collins\n- Events: Louisiana lieutenant gubernatorial election, 2015; Louisiana gubernatorial election, 2015\n- Roles: Louisiana lieutenant governor, Louisiana governor, United States Senator\n- Projects: Patient Freedom Act of 2017\n- Topics: United States healthcare reform, Affordable Care Act\n\nFacts:\n- In 2015, Billy Nungesser won the Louisiana lieutenant gubernatorial election by defeating Kip Holden.\n- In 2015, Democrat John Bel Edwards defeated David Vitter in the Louisiana gubernatorial election by a margin similar to Billy Nungesser's lieutenant gubernatorial victory.\n- David Vitter, born May 3, 1961, served as a United States Senator for Louisiana from 2005 to 2017.\n- On January 23, 2017, senators Susan Collins of Maine and Bill Cassidy of Louisiana proposed the Patient Freedom Act of 2017 as a United States healthcare plan to replace the Affordable Care Act.\n- In 2017, Bill Cassidy became Louisiana's senior senator when David Vitter retired.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
